# CommonMark parser

`cmark` is a CommonMark 0.31.2 command-line parser. It reads UTF-8 Markdown
from standard input and writes rendered HTML to standard output.

Run the complete supplied conformance suite with `sh full_test.sh`:

```sh
sh full_test.sh
```
#!/bin/sh
set -eu

SCRIPT_DIR=$(CDPATH= cd -- "$(dirname -- "$0")" && pwd)
exec python3 "$SCRIPT_DIR/sources/spec_tests.py" \
    --program "$SCRIPT_DIR/cmark" \
    --spec "$SCRIPT_DIR/sources/spec.txt"
#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Compatibility entry point for the supplied CommonMark conformance harness."""

import runpy


if __name__ == "__main__":
    runpy.run_path("cmark", run_name="__main__")

